# Translation
*.ko.md
# Korean translation mirror of the manual bundle. Owned by an external pipeline; this
# repository never tracks, edits or regenerates it. The `*.ko.md` rule above does not
# cover these, because the mirror uses plain filenames inside a `ko/` directory.
**/ko/
*.ko.txt

# Review/issue indexer pipeline output
issues_blocks.json

# Machine-local configuration, untracked by owner ruling 2026-09-02.
# Both pin absolute paths that are meaningful on exactly one machine, and a
# tracked absolute path is a trap for anyone else who clones. `.example`
# siblings are tracked in their place.
#
# `.cargo/config.toml` is NOT inert: it redirects `target-dir`, and
# CARGO_TARGET_DIR is unset on the owner's machine, so that file is what
# actually directs every build there. Untracking leaves it on disk; it must
# not be deleted.
/.unified-archive.toml

# The entire `.cargo/` directory is a cargo HOME that materialised inside the
# repository (registry cache, git checkouts, installed binaries — gigabytes of
# it). Only `config.toml` was ever meant to be here, and it is machine-local
# too. Ignore the directory's contents wholesale and re-admit just the example,
# so a stray `git add -A` can never sweep the cache in again.
#
# `.cargo/config.toml` is NOT inert: it redirects `target-dir`, and
# CARGO_TARGET_DIR is unset on the owner's machine, so that file is what
# actually directs every build there. It stays on disk; it must not be deleted.
/.cargo/*
!/.cargo/config.toml.example
